+## Guide: Introducing a new configuration option
+
+`zbarcam` accepts scanner and decoder configs via `-S<CONFIG>[=<VALUE>]` and `--set <CONFIG>[=<VALUE>]` (syntax: `[<symbology>.][no-]<config>[=<value>]`). These flow from `zbarcam/zbarcam.c` through `zbar_processor_parse_config()` -> `zbar_parse_config()` (`zbar/config.c`) -> `zbar_processor_set_config()` (`zbar/processor.c`) -> `zbar_image_scanner_set_config()` (`zbar/img_scanner.c`) -> `zbar_decoder_set_config()` (`zbar/decoder.c`).
+
+Note on naming: `TEST_CFG` in `zbar/decoder.h` and `zbar/img_scanner.c` is a bitmask-check macro (`((config >> cfg) & 1)`) for reading boolean configuration flags at runtime — it does **not** relate to unit testing or testing the code.
+
+### 1. Choose a category and add the enum value (`include/zbar.h`)
+
+`zbar_config_t` is partitioned into numeric ranges bounded by `ZBAR_CFG_*_START` / `ZBAR_CFG_*_END` delimiters that determine routing, array sizing, and indexing:
+
+| Category | Enum Range | Scope | Storage |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| Decoder boolean | `ZBAR_CFG_DEC_BOOL_START` (`0x00`) .. `ZBAR_CFG_DEC_BOOL_END` (`ZBAR_CFG_NUM`) | Per-symbology (or all) | Bit in decoder's `unsigned config` |
+| Decoder integer | `ZBAR_CFG_DEC_INT_START` (`0x20`) .. `ZBAR_CFG_DEC_INT_END` | Per-symbology (or all) | `int configs[NUM_CFGS]` in decoder |
+| Image-scanner per-symbology int | `ZBAR_CFG_SYM_INT_START` (`0x40`) .. `ZBAR_CFG_SYM_INT_END` | Per-symbology (or all) | `iscn->sym_configs[NUM_SYM_CFGS][NUM_SYMS]` |
+| Image-scanner global boolean | `ZBAR_CFG_SCN_BOOL_START` (`0x80`) .. `ZBAR_CFG_SCN_BOOL_END` | Scanner-wide (`sym <= ZBAR_PARTIAL`) | Bit in `iscn->config` |
+| Image-scanner global integer | `ZBAR_CFG_SCN_INT_START` (`0x100`) .. `ZBAR_CFG_SCN_INT_END` | Scanner-wide (`sym <= ZBAR_PARTIAL`) | `iscn->configs[NUM_SCN_CFGS]` |
+
+Add the new `ZBAR_CFG_*` constant to `enum zbar_config_e` right before the matching `*_END` delimiter (for decoder booleans, before `ZBAR_CFG_NUM`). Array sizes and range checks update automatically.
+
+### 2. Parse the config name (`zbar/config.c`)
+
+In `zbar_parse_config()`, add a `strncmp` branch mapping the CLI name to the new `ZBAR_CFG_*` value:
+
+- Matching is prefix-based and grouped by minimum unambiguous length (`len < 1`, `len < 2`, `len < 3`, ...); place the new check in the appropriate group so it neither shadows nor is shadowed by existing names.
+- `no-` negation and `=<value>` parsing (defaulting to `1` when omitted) are handled automatically.
+
+### 3. Store, validate, default, and read the setting
+
+- **Decoder boolean (`[ZBAR_CFG_DEC_BOOL_START, ZBAR_CFG_DEC_BOOL_END)`)**:
+  - Storage and validation (`0` or `1`) are handled automatically by `decoder_set_config_bool()` in `zbar/decoder.c`.
+  - Set non-zero defaults via `1 << ZBAR_CFG_...` in `zbar_decoder_create()` (`zbar/decoder.c`).
+  - Read with `TEST_CFG(dcode->mydec.config, ZBAR_CFG_...)` (the bitmask macro in `zbar/decoder.h`).
+- **Decoder integer (`[ZBAR_CFG_DEC_INT_START, ZBAR_CFG_DEC_INT_END)`)**:
+  - `NUM_CFGS` (`zbar/decoder.h`) and the range check in `zbar_decoder_set_config()` (`zbar/decoder.c`) update automatically from the enum delimiters.
+  - `decoder_set_config_int()` assigns `CFG(dcode->foo, cfg) = val;` for supported decoders.
+  - Set defaults in `zbar_decoder_create()` and read with `CFG(dcode->foo, ZBAR_CFG_...)`.
+- **Image-scanner per-symbology int (`[ZBAR_CFG_SYM_INT_START, ZBAR_CFG_SYM_INT_END)`)**:
+  - `NUM_SYM_CFGS` and the range check in `zbar_image_scanner_set_config()` (`zbar/img_scanner.c`) update automatically from the enum delimiters.
+  - Add any value validation in `zbar_image_scanner_set_config()`, set defaults in `zbar_image_scanner_create()`, and read via `SYM_CFG(iscn, ZBAR_CFG_..., h)`.
+- **Image-scanner global boolean (`[ZBAR_CFG_SCN_BOOL_START, ZBAR_CFG_SCN_BOOL_END)`)**:
+  - The range check in `zbar_image_scanner_set_config()` updates automatically from the enum delimiters.
+  - Set defaults in `zbar_image_scanner_create()` and read via `TEST_CFG(iscn, ZBAR_CFG_...)` (the bitmask macro in `zbar/img_scanner.c`).
+- **Image-scanner global integer (`[ZBAR_CFG_SCN_INT_START, ZBAR_CFG_SCN_INT_END)`)**:
+  - `NUM_SCN_CFGS` and the range check in `zbar_image_scanner_set_config()` (`zbar/img_scanner.c`) update automatically from the enum delimiters.
+  - Set defaults in `zbar_image_scanner_create()` and read via `CFG(iscn, ZBAR_CFG_...)`.
+
+### 4. Notes and pitfalls
+
+- No changes are required in `zbarcam/zbarcam.c` or `zbar/processor.c` for `-S` / `--set` forwarding (optionally update `note_usage` in `zbarcam/zbarcam.c` if the option should be documented in CLI help).
+- Keep each category's `*_END` strictly below the next category's `*_START` so ranges do not overlap.
+- `zbar_image_scanner_set_config()` rejects any `cfg >= ZBAR_CFG_SYM_INT_END` (scanner-global configs) when a specific symbology (`sym > ZBAR_PARTIAL`) is given.
+- `zbar_decoder_reset()` preserves decoder config fields across frames; ensure custom fields tied to a config are not cleared in `*_reset()` or `*_new_scan()`.
